S</given-names></name><name><surname>Mao</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Clues to the aetiological heterogeneity of testicular seminomas and non- seminomas: time trends and age-period-cohort effects</article-title><source>Int J Epidemiol</source><year>2000</year><volume>29</volume><fpage>826</fpage><lpage>831</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Int J Epidemiol||29|826||bib17|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11034964</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib18"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lunde</surname><given-names>AS</given-names></name><name><surname>Lundeberg</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Lettenstrom</surname><given-names>GS</given-names></name><name><surname>Thygesen</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Huebner</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title/><year>1980</year><publisher-name>National Center for Health Statistics: Hyattsville, MD</publisher-name>The person number systems of Sweden, Norway, Denmark and Israel, DHHS Publ NO. (PHS)80-1358. Vital and health statistics, series 2, No. 84: 5-11</citation></ref><ref id="bib19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mars&#x000c4;l</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Persson</surname><given-names>PH</given-names></name><name><surname>Larsen</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Lilja</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Selbing</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Sultan</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Intrauterine growth curves based on ultrasonically estimated foetal weights</article-title><source>Acta Paediatr</source><year>1996</year><volume>85</volume><fpage>843</fpage><lpage>848</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Acta Paediatr||85|843||bib19|'--><pub-id p